⍝ SKIlark: Joy's kernel on Scott data, interpreted by a fuelled fold
⍝ (PLAN.md).  The words are Joy's (von Thun) and the basis follows
⍝ Kerby; `Do` is Joy's `i`, since `I` is reserved for the combinator, and
⍝ `Ifz` is the one data-inspecting word, the Scott eliminator of nat.
⍝ `Qcons` is Joy's `cons`: `Cons` names the path constructor by SKIjack's
⍝ rule (SPEC section 8) and constructor names are global.
⍝ Quotations are data: `Quot` holds a program, not a function, so every
⍝ field is first-order and `Do` is a splice.  Derived words are equations
⍝ whose values are programs: the program's own names are its dictionary.
nat    ≡ Zero | Suc nat
item   ≡ Num nat | Quot prog
stack  ≡ Empty | Push item stack
word   ≡ Dup | Swap | Pop | Qcons | Cat | Unit | Dip | Do | Ifz | Lit nat | Quote prog | Add
prog   ≡ Done | Then word prog
result ≡ RVal stack | RErr | RTime

add m n = n ▹ { Zero m; Suc k (Suc (add m k)) }
mul m n = n ▹ { Zero Zero; Suc k (add m (mul m k)) }
cat p q = p ▹ { Done q; Then w r (Then w (cat r q)) }
⍝ the word that pushes an item back: cons, unit and dip re-quote a datum
wordOf a = a ▹ { Num n (Lit n); Quot r (Quote r) }

⍝ One unit of fuel per word.  step takes the loop as a parameter: the
⍝ expander ties one fixpoint per equation and refuses mutual recursion.
exec f p s = f ▹ { Zero RTime; Suc g (p ▹ { Done (RVal s); Then w q (step (exec g) w q s) }) }
step ex w q s = w ▹ {
  Dup     (s ▹ { Empty RErr; Push a t (ex q (Push a (Push a t))) });
  Swap    (s ▹ { Empty RErr; Push a t (t ▹ { Empty RErr; Push b u (ex q (Push b (Push a u))) }) });
  Pop     (s ▹ { Empty RErr; Push a t (ex q t) });
  Qcons   (s ▹ { Empty RErr; Push a t (a ▹ { Num n RErr; Quot r (t ▹ { Empty RErr; Push b u (ex q (Push (Quot (Then (wordOf b) r)) u)) }) }) });
  Cat     (s ▹ { Empty RErr; Push a t (a ▹ { Num n RErr; Quot r (t ▹ { Empty RErr; Push b u (b ▹ { Num m RErr; Quot l (ex q (Push (Quot (cat l r)) u)) }) }) }) });
  Unit    (s ▹ { Empty RErr; Push a t (ex q (Push (Quot (Then (wordOf a) Done)) t)) });
  Dip     (s ▹ { Empty RErr; Push a t (a ▹ { Num n RErr; Quot r (t ▹ { Empty RErr; Push b u (ex (cat r (Then (wordOf b) q)) u) }) }) });
  Do      (s ▹ { Empty RErr; Push a t (a ▹ { Num n RErr; Quot r (ex (cat r q) t) }) });
  Ifz     (s ▹ { Empty RErr; Push a t (a ▹ { Num n RErr; Quot sc (t ▹ { Empty RErr; Push b u (b ▹ { Num n RErr; Quot z (u ▹ { Empty RErr; Push c v (c ▹ { Num n (n ▹ { Zero (ex (cat z q) v); Suc m (ex (cat sc q) (Push (Num m) v)) }); Quot r RErr }) }) }) }) }) });
  Lit n   (ex q (Push (Num n) s));
  Quote r (ex q (Push (Quot r) s));
  Add     (s ▹ { Empty RErr; Push a t (t ▹ { Empty RErr; Push b u (a ▹ { Num m (b ▹ { Num n (ex q (Push (Num (add m n)) u)); Quot r RErr }); Quot r RErr }) }) }) }

⍝ The same loop without fuel, for level 1: there the interpreter's
⍝ fuel bounds the run, so the object program needs none of its own.
execU p s = p ▹ { Done (RVal s); Then w q (step execU w q s) }

one   ≔ Suc Zero
two   ≔ Suc one
three ≔ Suc two
five  ≔ add two three
ten   ≔ add five five
fuel  ≔ mul ten (add ten ten)

⍝ derived words, Joy's definitions
over  ≔ Then (Quote (Then Dup Done)) (Then Dip (Then Swap Done))
nip   ≔ Then (Quote (Then Pop Done)) (Then Dip Done)
tuck  ≔ Then Dup (Then (Quote (Then Swap Done)) (Then Dip Done))
rot   ≔ Then (Quote (Then Swap Done)) (Then Dip (Then Swap Done))
sip   ≔ Then (Quote (Then Dup Done)) (Then Dip (Then Dip Done))
kComb ≔ Then (Quote (Then Pop Done)) (Then Dip (Then Do Done))
⍝ Kerby's y: [P] y leaves [self] on top and runs P
yComb ≔ Then (Quote (Then Dup (Then Qcons Done))) (Then Swap (Then Cat (Then Dup (Then Qcons (Then Do Done)))))

⍝ sumto: n -> 0 + 1 + ... + n, by y.  With n [self] on the stack:
⍝   swap [pop 0] [dup [swap i] dip 1 + +] ifz
sumStep ≔ Then Dup (Then (Quote (Then Swap (Then Do Done))) (Then Dip (Then (Lit one) (Then Add (Then Add Done)))))
sumBody ≔ Then Swap (Then (Quote (Then Pop (Then (Lit Zero) Done))) (Then (Quote sumStep) (Then Ifz Done)))
sumto   ≔ Then (Quote sumBody) yComb

⍝ programs; stacks are written bottom to top
p1 ≔ Then (Lit one) (Then (Lit two) (Then Add (Then Dup (Then Add Done))))          ⍝ 1 2 + dup +      => 6
p2 ≔ Then (Lit three) (Then (Quote (Then Dup (Then Add Done))) (Then Do Done))       ⍝ 3 [dup +] i      => 6
p3 ≔ Then (Lit one) (Then (Lit two) over)                                            ⍝ 1 2 over         => 1 2 1
p4 ≔ Then (Lit one) (Then (Quote (Then (Lit two) Done)) (Then (Quote (Then (Lit three) Done)) kComb))  ⍝ 1 [2] [3] k => 1 3
p5 ≔ Then (Lit one) (Then (Lit two) (Then Unit (Then Qcons Done)))                    ⍝ 1 2 unit cons    => [1 2]
p6 ≔ Then Add Done                                                                   ⍝ +                => RErr
p7 ≔ Then (Lit three) sumto                                                          ⍝ 3 sumto          => 6
p8 ≔ Then (Lit five) sumto                                                           ⍝ 5 sumto          => 15
r1 ≔ exec fuel p1 Empty
r2 ≔ exec fuel p2 Empty
r3 ≔ exec fuel p3 Empty
r4 ≔ exec fuel p4 Empty
r5 ≔ exec fuel p5 Empty
r6 ≔ exec fuel p6 Empty
r7 ≔ exec fuel p7 Empty
r8 ≔ exec fuel p8 Empty
r8starved ≔ exec ten p8 Empty

⍝ the algebra of programs, each law on a sample stack; the tests compare
⍝ the two sides' results
lawSwapL ≔ Then (Lit one) (Then (Lit two) (Then Swap (Then Swap Done)))
lawSwapR ≔ Then (Lit one) (Then (Lit two) Done)
lawDupL  ≔ Then (Lit one) (Then Dup (Then Pop Done))
lawDupR  ≔ Then (Lit one) Done
lawDoL   ≔ Then (Lit two) (Then (Quote (Then (Lit one) (Then Add Done))) (Then Do Done))
lawDoR   ≔ Then (Lit two) (Then (Lit one) (Then Add Done))
lawCatL  ≔ Then (Quote (Then (Lit one) Done)) (Then (Quote (Then (Lit two) Done)) (Then Cat Done))
lawCatR  ≔ Then (Quote (Then (Lit one) (Then (Lit two) Done))) Done
lawDipL  ≔ Then (Lit five) (Then (Quote (Then (Lit one) Done)) (Then (Quote (Then (Lit two) (Then Add Done))) (Then Dip Done)))
lawDipR  ≔ Then (Lit five) (Then (Lit two) (Then Add (Then (Quote (Then (Lit one) Done)) Done)))
lawUnitL ≔ Then (Lit one) (Then Unit Done)
lawUnitR ≔ Then (Quote (Then (Lit one) Done)) Done
lawKL    ≔ p4
lawKR    ≔ Then (Lit one) (Then (Lit three) Done)
lawSipL  ≔ Then (Quote (Then (Lit one) Done)) (Then (Quote (Then Do (Then (Lit two) (Then Add Done)))) sip)
lawSipR  ≔ Then (Quote (Then (Lit one) Done)) (Then Do (Then (Lit two) (Then Add (Then (Quote (Then (Lit one) Done)) Done))))
